WEBVTT

00:02.000 --> 00:05.077
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:05.145 --> 00:08.491
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.559 --> 00:11.636
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.705 --> 00:14.615
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.682 --> 00:18.564
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.632 --> 00:21.508
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.577 --> 00:23.116
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:23.184 --> 00:24.487
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.555 --> 00:27.667
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:36.500 --> 00:37.570
All right, come on,
hurry up, Brian.

00:37.641 --> 00:39.949
I don't want to miss the movie
trivia slides before the movie.

00:40.017 --> 00:41.756
Peter, those questions
are the easiest,

00:41.824 --> 00:43.330
most pandering things
in the world.

00:47.815 --> 00:49.419
Oh! Oh! Tim Honks!
Tim Honks!

00:49.488 --> 00:50.624
<i>Forrest Gump. I win.</i>

00:53.002 --> 00:54.640
Who?

00:56.917 --> 00:58.154
Ah, good.
It's starting.

00:58.222 --> 00:59.660
Yeah, that's what you say.

00:59.728 --> 01:02.204
I can never figure out when
the hell the studio logos end

01:02.272 --> 01:03.509
and the actual movie begins.

01:03.576 --> 01:04.981
(fanfare playing)

01:05.049 --> 01:07.190
All right. Let's see
what you got, FOX.

01:07.259 --> 01:10.101
Oh, I bet that's a sea monst...

01:10.170 --> 01:11.975
Oh, that's not the movie.

01:12.044 --> 01:14.351
That's... yeah, I think
I heard of them.

01:14.419 --> 01:17.197
Here we go. Movie!

01:17.264 --> 01:20.677
Well, now, that seems
intentionally misleading.

01:20.744 --> 01:23.621
All right, someone's
coming to town.

01:23.689 --> 01:26.868
Oh, for crying out loud.

01:26.936 --> 01:30.046
Oh, all right. Period movie.

01:30.115 --> 01:32.021
Oh, not a period movie.

01:34.498 --> 01:36.640
Oh, this guy's in trouble.

01:36.707 --> 01:38.312
Can't wait to hear his story.

01:40.087 --> 01:41.492
Oh, come on!

01:44.270 --> 01:46.044
Psst. Hey, Brian.
You want a drink?

01:46.111 --> 01:47.683
You snuck in liquor?

01:47.750 --> 01:50.661
Yeah, loosens me up so I can
talk to the people around me.

01:50.729 --> 01:52.368
All right, I'll, uh,
get in on that.

01:56.017 --> 01:58.760
(slurring words): Hey, I
already seen this movie.

01:58.828 --> 02:01.804
Let's talk... let's talk about
other movies we've seen.

02:01.873 --> 02:03.378
That's an excellent idea.

02:03.446 --> 02:05.888
<i>I like... I like The Madness
of King George.</i>

02:05.956 --> 02:07.662
Well, I don't know
what that is,

02:07.729 --> 02:09.503
<i>but The... The Cat
From Outer Space</i>

02:09.570 --> 02:11.610
is a solid
motion picture.

02:11.678 --> 02:13.852
<i>Oh, and... and I like...
I like King Ralph</i>

02:13.920 --> 02:15.627
'cause... 'cause that's...
that's the last guy

02:15.695 --> 02:17.935
you'd expect to be
king of nothing.

02:18.003 --> 02:19.408
Hey, shut up!

02:19.476 --> 02:21.515
Hey, I'm... I'm not
the only one talking.

02:21.584 --> 02:24.160
That... that big guy up
there on the screen's

02:24.228 --> 02:26.034
been talking through
the whole movie.

02:26.102 --> 02:27.908
Hey, jerk. Hey,
you keep it down.

02:27.976 --> 02:30.083
I-I don't...
I don't think he's...

02:30.152 --> 02:32.291
that he's listening to you.
Let's get him.

02:32.360 --> 02:34.534
Dear Liesl, I'd like
to be able to tell you

02:34.603 --> 02:35.973
how I feel about you.

02:36.040 --> 02:39.521
Leeza, get a... get away
from him. He's a "Nazzi."

02:39.588 --> 02:42.431
I-I know Jews is bad,
but thems is worse.

02:42.500 --> 02:43.871
Sit down!
Move.

02:43.939 --> 02:45.610
Stop blocking
the screen, you jerk!

02:45.679 --> 02:48.121
I don't think... I don't
think you heard me, buddy.

02:48.189 --> 02:49.761
Step away from
the young lady.

02:51.837 --> 02:54.479
All right, Ian Ziering,
you asked for it.

02:56.790 --> 02:59.968
Oh, my God.
I think I'm in Narnia.

03:00.035 --> 03:01.506
Where am I?

03:01.575 --> 03:03.381
Hey, those guys
are backwards now.

03:03.449 --> 03:04.719
Get away from her!

03:07.431 --> 03:09.471
We got a report
of a disturban...

03:09.539 --> 03:11.480
Oh, what the hell, Peter?

03:11.547 --> 03:13.756
Joe, thank God.
There's a situation here.

03:13.823 --> 03:15.461
I've got a sore finger.

03:15.530 --> 03:17.570
I don't give a crap.
We got bigger problems!

03:21.754 --> 03:23.796
Mr. Griffin
and Mr. Griffin,

03:23.863 --> 03:26.873
this court finds you guilty
of creating a public disturbance

03:26.941 --> 03:28.814
and destruction
of private property.

03:28.882 --> 03:32.028
And all of this while under
the influence of alcohol.

03:32.096 --> 03:34.269
Your Honor, if you'll
just let us explain...

03:34.337 --> 03:36.712
I've heard all the testimony
I'm prepared to hear.

03:36.780 --> 03:38.686
This court sentences you both

03:38.755 --> 03:41.632
to 30 days
of Alcoholics Anonymous.

03:41.700 --> 03:43.606
Well, Your Honor, in that case,

03:43.673 --> 03:46.250
I'll have to call my surprise
witness, Mr. Sockerby.

03:46.318 --> 03:47.589
Mr. Sockerby, before we begin,

03:47.657 --> 03:49.496
have you ever been convicted
of a felony?

03:49.564 --> 03:51.170
Yes, but that bitch
had it coming.

03:51.237 --> 03:53.344
Ah, okay. Uh, Your Honor, I'm...

03:53.412 --> 03:55.419
I'm afraid I have
to withdraw this witness,

03:55.487 --> 03:58.598
and I am going to those things
you said I have to go to.

04:04.616 --> 04:06.188
This sucks.
Can't believe that judge

04:06.256 --> 04:08.095
is making us go
to a month of AA.

04:08.163 --> 04:10.404
You know, if you ask me,
this is going to be

04:10.473 --> 04:11.844
a good thing for
both of you.

04:11.912 --> 04:13.249
There's a lesson
you need to learn.

04:13.317 --> 04:14.420
What are you talking about?
What lesson?

04:14.488 --> 04:15.994
I don't need to go to AA.

04:16.061 --> 04:17.433
I'm a social drinker,
not an alcoholic.

04:17.500 --> 04:20.076
Yeah, that's like saying rappers
are really poets.

04:22.052 --> 04:26.034
I'm not saying she's
a gold digger,

04:26.101 --> 04:29.581
but she's not messing with...

04:29.648 --> 04:32.592
Who isn't she messing with?

04:36.242 --> 04:37.678
Hey, y'all.

04:37.746 --> 04:41.126
Okay, we got us a few new
friends here joining us tonight.

04:41.194 --> 04:45.276
So let's all say us
a big hello to Peter and Brian.

04:45.343 --> 04:47.986
ALL: Hello, Peter and Brian.
Hi there.

04:48.054 --> 04:50.262
All right, who'd like
to kick us off?

04:50.330 --> 04:51.801
I will.

04:51.869 --> 04:55.249
Um, my name is Greg,
and, uh, I'm an alcoholic.

04:55.317 --> 04:56.821
ALL:
Hi, Greg.

04:56.889 --> 04:59.733
One fateful night, I, uh,
got behind the wheel

04:59.801 --> 05:02.509
of my brand-new sports car,
blind-drunk.

05:02.578 --> 05:04.685
I was responsible for the death

05:04.754 --> 05:06.492
of an innocent
eight-year-old girl.

05:06.560 --> 05:07.897
What kind?
What?

05:07.966 --> 05:09.337
What kind of car?

05:09.405 --> 05:11.144
You said you had
a sports car.

05:11.212 --> 05:12.048
That's cool,
but what kind?

05:12.116 --> 05:13.320
It was a Miata.

05:13.388 --> 05:15.060
Oh, come on. That's
not a sports car.

05:15.128 --> 05:16.867
How... how does that
even kill a kid?

05:16.934 --> 05:19.143
What, did you hit her
over the head with it?

05:19.210 --> 05:20.649
That's a legitimate sports car.
No. Next.

05:20.717 --> 05:23.058
Jenny, would you
like to talk?

05:23.125 --> 05:25.701
My name is Jenny,
and I'm an alcoholic.

05:25.769 --> 05:27.542
Geez, anybody here
in any other line of work?

05:27.610 --> 05:28.881
Ha.

05:28.949 --> 05:30.420
ALL:
Hi, Jenny.

05:30.488 --> 05:33.131
Before I found AA,
my ex-boyfriend and I

05:33.199 --> 05:34.737
used to get drunk
and party all night.

05:34.805 --> 05:36.410
I missed work half the time.

05:36.478 --> 05:38.887
One morning, I woke up naked
with three Persians

05:38.955 --> 05:41.162
high-fiving each other
on the way out of my bedroom.

05:41.230 --> 05:42.903
But now that I've joined
the program,

05:42.971 --> 05:44.744
I'm a whole different person.

05:44.812 --> 05:46.550
And my two new cats,
Clean and Sober,

05:46.618 --> 05:48.391
just think I'm tops.

05:48.459 --> 05:50.097
That's wonderful,
Jenny.

05:50.166 --> 05:53.411
All right. Peter, do you have a
story that you'd like to share?

05:53.479 --> 05:54.782
Oh, yeah, I got one.

05:54.850 --> 05:57.025
This one time, me and Joe
and Quagmire made a bet

05:57.092 --> 05:59.402
to see who could drink
the most beer and still drive.

05:59.469 --> 06:01.743
And you know that water slide
in South Attleboro?

06:07.868 --> 06:09.708
Yeah!
Water slide!

06:09.775 --> 06:11.482
Summer fun!

06:12.855 --> 06:14.996
Peter, it sounds to me
like alcohol

06:15.063 --> 06:17.941
is a very destructive
influence in your life.

06:18.009 --> 06:19.681
You need to relinquish
your dependence

06:19.749 --> 06:22.492
and give yourself over
to a higher power.

06:22.560 --> 06:25.136
(scoffs) You have a
different view, Brian?

06:25.203 --> 06:26.441
Oh, I-I don't know.
Are we...

06:26.509 --> 06:28.048
are we allowed to have
a different view?

06:28.115 --> 06:31.494
Brian, AA is the only way out
for these people.

06:31.562 --> 06:34.606
Millions are saved every year
by the program.

06:34.674 --> 06:36.045
Hey, people got along just fine

06:36.113 --> 06:38.053
for thousands of years
without AA.

06:38.122 --> 06:39.425
Just like they got along

06:39.493 --> 06:41.232
for thousands of years
without religion.

06:41.301 --> 06:43.508
I like you and have
no reason not to.

06:43.576 --> 06:45.516
I like you and have
no reason not to.

06:45.584 --> 06:47.524
Hey, did you hear
about that magic baby

06:47.592 --> 06:48.695
that was born
in Bethlehem?

06:48.763 --> 06:50.603
(all yelling)

06:56.862 --> 06:58.166
Oh, there you boys are.

06:58.233 --> 06:59.571
How was your meeting?

06:59.639 --> 07:01.814
29 more and we're done--
that's how it was.

07:01.881 --> 07:03.787
That doesn't sound like
the right attitude.

07:03.856 --> 07:05.729
Lois, you weren't there.
It was awful.

07:05.797 --> 07:08.272
Just a bunch of losers
telling boring stories.

07:08.340 --> 07:10.112
"My drinking
ruined my marriage."

07:10.181 --> 07:12.155
"My drinking ruined
my family."

07:12.223 --> 07:15.234
<i>My drinking
ruined my TV show, 24."</i>

07:15.301 --> 07:17.509
I see you got your own thing
going on this week,

07:17.576 --> 07:18.981
but there's a new teacher
at preschool

07:19.049 --> 07:21.291
who deactivates the camera
and then hits us.

07:21.359 --> 07:23.566
Brian, AA's been around
for years.

07:23.634 --> 07:26.076
It's helped a lot of people
get over their addiction.

07:26.144 --> 07:27.514
No, it hasn't.

07:27.582 --> 07:29.021
They've just traded
one addiction for another.

07:29.088 --> 07:30.694
Their life goes
from being all about drinking

07:30.762 --> 07:31.966
to being all about AA.

07:32.034 --> 07:33.505
The only difference is,

07:33.573 --> 07:35.279
when it's all about drinking,
they're more fun.

07:35.347 --> 07:36.483
Well, like
it or not,

07:36.552 --> 07:39.596
you got to stick it
out for 30 days.

07:39.663 --> 07:40.834
You know what sucks, Brian?

07:40.902 --> 07:42.674
We don't got a problem
with our drinking.

07:42.742 --> 07:44.883
It's everybody else who's got
a problem with our drinking.

07:44.951 --> 07:46.924
Wait a minute.
Peter, that's it.

07:46.993 --> 07:49.166
The issue isn't that these
people are alcoholics.

07:49.235 --> 07:52.078
They just have nowhere to
drink without being judged.

07:52.146 --> 07:53.818
She slams us
into the monkey bars,

07:53.886 --> 07:56.663
but none of us have the language
skills to call her on it.

07:59.943 --> 08:01.783
And then this one time,
I was so drunk,

08:01.850 --> 08:03.624
I gave someone
a back adjustment.

08:03.692 --> 08:04.996
I'm not a chiropractor.

08:05.064 --> 08:07.037
You got to go to a weekend
of school for that.

08:07.105 --> 08:08.476
Hey, hey.

08:08.544 --> 08:10.820
Anyone in the house
addicted to alcohol?

08:10.887 --> 08:12.191
Hi.
Hello, Peter.

08:12.258 --> 08:13.563
I enjoy alcohol.

08:13.630 --> 08:15.437
I can't hear you.

08:15.505 --> 08:17.847
Me. Hello.
I have a very serious problem.

08:17.914 --> 08:21.126
Mr. Griffin, alcohol
is forbidden at our meetings.

08:21.193 --> 08:22.565
Look, j-just hear me out.

08:22.633 --> 08:24.941
I sat here and listened
to you bums the other day,

08:25.009 --> 08:27.685
and I got to tell you,
I have never seen a duller bunch

08:27.753 --> 08:29.091
of pathetic bastards in my life.

08:29.159 --> 08:30.864
I don't know who you were
when you were drinking,

08:30.932 --> 08:32.404
but it sure as hell's
got to be better

08:32.472 --> 08:33.441
than who you are
when you're sober.

08:33.509 --> 08:34.747
Yeah, you all stopped drinking

08:34.815 --> 08:36.386
because you were hurting
your loved ones.

08:36.453 --> 08:38.896
But you can't hurt them
if they don't know you're drunk.

08:38.964 --> 08:41.406
Let's make this our sanctuary.

08:43.013 --> 08:45.054
I wants me that beer.

08:51.078 --> 08:52.818
MAN (over radio):
Attention, patrol cars,

08:52.886 --> 08:55.562
we've got a noise complaint
at the Quahog Community Center.

08:55.630 --> 08:57.235
Is anyone in the area?

08:57.303 --> 08:59.478
Wait a minute. That's where
Peter's AA meeting is.

09:05.234 --> 09:06.873
So I clicked
on it, and the...

09:06.941 --> 09:09.283
the girl's got
a bigger wang than I got.

09:09.351 --> 09:10.386
No way.

09:10.454 --> 09:11.591
No way, right?

09:11.659 --> 09:13.801
So I did... so I just put
my thumb over it,

09:13.868 --> 09:16.578
and then... and that got me
through the rest of...

09:16.646 --> 09:19.489
of the... of the session.

09:24.744 --> 09:27.722
Oh, no.
There's a policeman coming.

09:27.790 --> 09:29.027
(all gasping)

09:29.094 --> 09:30.700
All right, everybody,
you know what to do.

09:30.768 --> 09:33.713
Alcoholics, transform.

09:44.656 --> 09:46.998
All right, what the hell's
going on in here?

09:47.066 --> 09:50.043
We got a noise complaint. Joe, shh.
Peter's about to start.

09:50.111 --> 09:53.490
We are gathered here again
tonight, fellow AA members,

09:53.557 --> 09:55.230
to talk about
the greatest temptation

09:55.298 --> 09:56.536
the Devil ever created--

09:56.604 --> 09:57.941
alcohol.

09:58.009 --> 09:59.044
(humming tune)

09:59.113 --> 10:01.421
♪ Mr. Booze ♪

10:01.489 --> 10:03.195
<i>♪ Mr. Booze ♪</i>

10:03.263 --> 10:05.437
♪ Mr. Booze ♪

10:05.505 --> 10:09.754
♪ Mr. B-double-O-Z-E ♪

10:09.821 --> 10:14.339
<i>♪ That sure spells booze ♪</i>

10:14.407 --> 10:17.150
♪ You will wind up wearing
tattered shoes ♪

10:17.219 --> 10:19.727
♪ If you mess with Mr. Booze ♪

10:19.795 --> 10:22.003
<i>♪ Don't mess with Mr. Booze ♪</i>

10:23.475 --> 10:25.884
<i>♪ Don't mess with Mr. Booze ♪</i>

10:25.952 --> 10:27.791
♪ Don't mess with
B-double-O-Z-E ♪

10:27.859 --> 10:31.306
♪ If you've been so stiff
they thought you died ♪

10:31.374 --> 10:34.819
♪ You'll feel better
once you've testified ♪

10:34.887 --> 10:37.329
♪ Testify ♪
♪ Oh, yeah ♪

10:37.397 --> 10:39.739
♪ Testify ♪
I want to testify.
I want to testify.

10:39.807 --> 10:42.349
Well, then, cleanse yourself,
my son. Cleanse yourself.

10:42.417 --> 10:44.558
One time, I took
a "liberry" book out,

10:44.626 --> 10:47.436
and I fells asleep reading it,
and I left it under the bed.

10:47.503 --> 10:50.046
I forgot about it
for three and a half years.

10:50.114 --> 10:52.622
I was going to take it back
on Amnesty Day,

10:52.690 --> 10:55.033
but on Amnesty Day,
I had a sip of ros├й wine,

10:55.101 --> 10:57.308
and I never made it
out of the house.

10:57.376 --> 10:59.182
<i>♪ Who's to blame? ♪
♪ Who's to blame? ♪</i>

10:59.250 --> 11:00.789
<i>♪ What's his name? ♪
♪ We know his name ♪</i>

11:00.857 --> 11:03.064
♪ His name is Mr. Booze ♪

11:03.132 --> 11:04.504
♪ Mr. Booze ♪

11:04.571 --> 11:07.949
♪ Mr. B-double-O-Z-E,
don't ever choose ♪

11:08.018 --> 11:11.430
♪ Any game you play
with him you lose ♪

11:11.498 --> 11:14.342
♪ So don't mess with Mr. Booze ♪

11:14.410 --> 11:18.827
<i>♪ If your head feels
like it's two miles wide ♪
♪ Two miles wide ♪</i>

11:18.894 --> 11:23.211
<i>♪ You'll feel better
once you've testified ♪
♪ Testify ♪</i>

11:23.278 --> 11:25.118
<i>♪ Oh, yes ♪
♪ Testify ♪</i>

11:25.186 --> 11:27.292
I want to testify.
I want to testify.

11:27.361 --> 11:29.636
Well, come forward,
dear brother, and testify.

11:29.704 --> 11:31.308
I used to be a
soda pop guy.

11:31.376 --> 11:32.781
Then I switched
to the bottle.

11:32.849 --> 11:34.087
Now I don't
leave my couch,

11:34.154 --> 11:35.391
and I've seen
every movie ever.

11:35.459 --> 11:37.031
You name a movie,
I've seen it.

11:37.099 --> 11:38.538
<i>Meet Dave.
Seen it.</i>

11:38.605 --> 11:40.111
<i>The Eiger Sanction.
Seen it.</i>

11:40.178 --> 11:41.716
<i>Donovan's Reef.
Seen it.</i>

11:41.784 --> 11:44.092
<i>License to Drive.
Definitely seen it.</i>

11:44.161 --> 11:45.933
<i>♪ That's a shame ♪
♪ What a shame ♪</i>

11:46.000 --> 11:47.439
<i>♪ Who's to blame? ♪
♪ For Corey Haim? ♪</i>

11:47.507 --> 11:51.254
♪ His name is Mr. Booze,
Mr. Booze ♪

11:51.322 --> 11:54.500
♪ Mr. B-double-O-Z-E,
you must refuse ♪

11:54.568 --> 11:57.713
♪ You'll make
the obituary news ♪

11:57.780 --> 12:01.629
♪ If you mess with Mr. Booze ♪

12:01.696 --> 12:05.109
♪ If you've been so stiff
they thought you died ♪

12:05.176 --> 12:08.455
♪ You'll feel better
once you've testified ♪

12:08.523 --> 12:11.098
♪ Testify, testify ♪

12:11.167 --> 12:13.174
This man wants
to testify.

12:13.242 --> 12:14.412
Very well, my brother.

12:14.479 --> 12:16.420
Let us lead him on the path
of righteousness.

12:16.487 --> 12:17.859
This poor gentleman
used to speak

12:17.927 --> 12:19.064
in long,
eloquent sentences,

12:19.132 --> 12:20.569
but after years
of drinking,

12:20.637 --> 12:22.611
he can only speak
in short, choppy utterances.

12:22.679 --> 12:24.250
Why, at one time,
if you asked him

12:24.318 --> 12:25.556
who his favorite
musicians were,

12:25.623 --> 12:28.266
he'd say Leonard Bernstein,
Johann Sebastian Bach

12:28.335 --> 12:29.940
and Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart.

12:30.007 --> 12:32.684
But thanks to that old devil
hooch, it's all changed.

12:32.753 --> 12:33.756
Who's your favorite
musician, Ollie?

12:33.822 --> 12:34.892
Cher!

12:34.961 --> 12:36.365
He doesn't even
like Cher.

12:36.433 --> 12:38.273
♪ Now, alcohol makes
a big man small ♪

12:38.341 --> 12:39.979
<i>♪ And can lead
to a life of crime ♪
♪ Yeah! ♪</i>

12:40.047 --> 12:41.452
♪ Demon rum makes
a gent a bum ♪

12:41.520 --> 12:43.159
♪ And you cash in
before your time ♪

12:43.227 --> 12:44.932
<i>♪ Yeah! ♪
♪ Bootleg gin
puts you in a spin ♪</i>

12:45.000 --> 12:46.472
<i>♪ Till you don't even
know your name ♪
♪ Yeah! ♪</i>

12:46.540 --> 12:48.145
♪ You're a basket case
flat on your face ♪

12:48.213 --> 12:49.584
♪ And there's only one guy
to blame ♪

12:49.652 --> 12:50.621
<i>♪ Mr. B-double-O-Z-E ♪</i>

12:50.689 --> 12:53.331
♪ Mr. Booze, Mr. Booze ♪

12:53.400 --> 12:56.779
♪ Mr. B-double-O-Z-E,
don't ever choose ♪

12:56.847 --> 12:59.623
♪ You will wind up wearing
tattered shoes ♪

12:59.691 --> 13:02.200
♪ If you mess with Mr. Booze ♪

13:02.269 --> 13:04.375
<i>♪ Don't mess with Mr. Booze ♪</i>

13:04.443 --> 13:05.714
♪ Oh, Mr. Booze ♪

13:05.782 --> 13:07.723
<i>♪ Don't mess with Mr. Booze ♪</i>

13:07.790 --> 13:08.960
♪ Oh, Mr. Booze ♪

13:09.028 --> 13:12.340
<i>♪ Don't mess with Mr. Booze ♪</i>

13:12.408 --> 13:15.118
♪ Don't mess
with B-double-O-Z-E ♪

13:15.185 --> 13:17.794
♪ 'Cause that spells booze ♪

13:17.863 --> 13:22.614
♪ And you gotta lose
with Mr. Booze ♪

13:22.682 --> 13:24.856
<i>♪ Oh, yeah ♪</i>

13:24.924 --> 13:29.139
♪ Don't mess around
with Mr. Booze ♪

13:29.207 --> 13:31.650
<i>♪ Don't mess with Mr. Booze ♪</i>

13:31.718 --> 13:34.997
<i>♪ That's what he said, now ♪
♪ Don't mess with Mr. Booze ♪</i>

13:35.064 --> 13:40.753
<i>♪ Oh, Mr. Booze ♪
♪ Don't mess with Mr. Booze ♪</i>

13:40.820 --> 13:44.869
<i>♪ Don't you mess with Mr. Booze,
don't mess with Mr. ♪</i>

13:44.936 --> 13:46.842
<i>♪ Don't you mess with Mr.,
oh-oh-oh-oh-oh-oh ♪</i>

13:46.910 --> 13:48.549
<i>♪ Don't mess with, ah-ah ♪</i>

13:48.618 --> 13:50.959
<i>♪ Oh, Mr. Booze ♪</i>

13:51.027 --> 13:54.238
<i>♪ Oh, yeah, oh, yeah, oh, yeah,
oh-oh-oh-oh-oh-oh ♪</i>

13:54.306 --> 13:56.614
<i>♪ Yeah! ♪</i>

13:56.682 --> 13:58.522
Wow, you guys.
I'm impressed

13:58.590 --> 14:00.698
that you're taking your
sentence so seriously.

14:00.766 --> 14:03.877
And I know that the court
will be happy to hear this, too.

14:03.945 --> 14:06.052
Now, if you'll just keep it down

14:06.121 --> 14:07.758
so I don't get
any more complaints.

14:07.826 --> 14:08.997
Sure. No problem, Joe.

14:09.065 --> 14:10.570
Thanks for stopping by.

14:12.410 --> 14:15.456
Yay!
(all cheer)

14:19.841 --> 14:21.044
So what do you say, guys?

14:21.112 --> 14:22.483
Should we take this party
to Denny's

14:22.551 --> 14:24.191
and hang out with the cast
of the high school play?

14:24.258 --> 14:26.364
Nah. I think I'm...
I'm just going to go home.

14:26.433 --> 14:27.771
All right.
You okay to drive?

14:27.838 --> 14:29.176
Oh, yeah, I'll be fine.

14:29.244 --> 14:30.983
I-I'll crank the heat,
roll up the windows

14:31.051 --> 14:32.656
and blast the Lullaby Channel.
I'll be fine.

14:32.724 --> 14:33.861
All right, take it easy.

14:33.929 --> 14:35.401
All right, you, too.
Get out of here.

14:35.468 --> 14:36.806
Hey! Like your jeans.

14:36.874 --> 14:38.078
Thanks. What...
hey, what size are you?

14:38.146 --> 14:39.819
Yeah, I don't think
we're the same size.

14:39.886 --> 14:41.290
Yeah, we'll figure
it out tomorrow.

14:41.359 --> 14:42.896
Come on, Brian.
You ready to go home?

14:42.965 --> 14:44.604
Uh, no, Peter.

14:44.672 --> 14:46.678
I'm going to... I'm going to...
going to meet Jenny's cats.

14:46.747 --> 14:48.419
What are you talking about?
You hate cats.

14:48.487 --> 14:50.928
I'm going... to meet...
her cats.

14:50.996 --> 14:52.401
Geez. All right.
Okay. All right.

14:52.469 --> 14:54.142
You don't have
to get all c-c-cat...

14:54.209 --> 14:56.082
Hey, hey, cat dog, right?

14:56.150 --> 14:57.755
You're a cat dog.

14:57.823 --> 14:59.262
♪ Hey, cat dog ♪

14:59.330 --> 15:01.069
♪ Cat dog ♪

15:01.136 --> 15:03.043
(sings gibberish)
♪ Cat dog. ♪

15:03.111 --> 15:04.415
Hey, where's...
you know,

15:04.483 --> 15:06.623
where's all the poop go
when the cat...

15:06.691 --> 15:08.263
when the...
in a... in a cat dog...?

15:08.332 --> 15:09.602
When the cat poops...

15:09.670 --> 15:11.543
what, does it come out
of the dog's mouth?

15:11.611 --> 15:13.418
And... and vice versa?

15:13.486 --> 15:15.023
Oh, God.

15:15.091 --> 15:17.869
Oh, that's... that's
some kind of living hell.

15:17.936 --> 15:19.742
That's some...

15:19.810 --> 15:22.420
that's some kind
of living hell, Brian.

15:22.487 --> 15:23.658
Okay, I got to go.

15:23.726 --> 15:25.364
You... you have
a good time with Jenny.

15:33.130 --> 15:34.868
(tires squeal)

15:39.186 --> 15:41.561
Geez. Cat dog.

15:41.629 --> 15:43.068
What-what if... what if they...

15:43.135 --> 15:44.975
what if they want
to marry different people?

15:45.042 --> 15:47.016
You got a lawsuit on your hands.

15:47.085 --> 15:48.856
That's what...
that's what happens.

15:48.924 --> 15:50.263
All right... all right, look,

15:50.330 --> 15:52.103
let's get some music
going on in here.

15:52.171 --> 15:53.542
Where's the Lullaby Channel?

15:53.609 --> 15:55.048
(soft music plays)

15:55.116 --> 15:57.993
♪ A gentle breeze ♪

15:58.061 --> 16:01.875
♪ From Hushabye Mountain ♪

16:01.943 --> 16:05.489
♪ Softly blows ♪

16:05.557 --> 16:09.304
♪ For Lullaby Bay. ♪

16:09.372 --> 16:10.776
(tires squealing)

16:16.902 --> 16:18.306
Please be
Rosie O'Donnell.

16:18.374 --> 16:21.519
Please be Rosie O'Donnell.
Please be Rosie O'Donnell.

16:21.587 --> 16:22.857
(sighs)

16:22.925 --> 16:24.698
Wait. Is it?

16:27.116 --> 16:27.817
Hey.

16:27.880 --> 16:29.853
Hey, fatty,
wake up.

16:34.406 --> 16:36.346
What... what the...
what happened?

16:36.414 --> 16:37.919
You're dead, jackass.

16:37.986 --> 16:40.094
You died in a drunk
driving accident.

16:40.162 --> 16:42.604
Oh, God. Did I hold on
to the touchdown pass?

16:42.672 --> 16:44.812
What the...?
What's wrong with you?

16:44.881 --> 16:45.917
You know what?

16:45.985 --> 16:47.556
I was so drunk,
my ghost is drunk.

16:47.624 --> 16:49.865
Look, I've been told
I can give you another chance,

16:49.934 --> 16:51.840
but there's some things
we have to do first.

16:51.908 --> 16:53.078
What are you
talking about?

16:53.146 --> 16:55.287
I'm talking about you
understanding alcohol

16:55.356 --> 16:56.927
just a little bit better.

16:56.995 --> 16:59.571
Peter, I'm going to show you
where your life is headed

16:59.639 --> 17:02.047
if you keep drinking
as much as you do.

17:02.115 --> 17:03.787
(whooshing)

17:05.797 --> 17:08.707
(whooshing)

17:08.775 --> 17:10.715
All right, Peter.
Here we are.

17:10.783 --> 17:12.019
Well, everything
looks fine.

17:14.732 --> 17:17.474
(slurring): All right, family.
Line up for cigar burns.

17:19.015 --> 17:19.951
Ah!

17:21.190 --> 17:22.762
Oh!

17:22.830 --> 17:24.737
Yow!

17:24.804 --> 17:26.209
Ah!

17:26.276 --> 17:28.117
Ah!

17:28.184 --> 17:29.823
Wait a minute.
Who are you?

17:29.891 --> 17:31.697
(British accent):
I'm your other son, MacCawber.

17:31.765 --> 17:33.873
Here for my cigar burn,
good sir.

17:33.940 --> 17:35.880
Stewie, go on,
get out of here,

17:35.948 --> 17:37.587
you stupid "laugh and cry,
effin' cry."

17:37.655 --> 17:38.591
What's the difference?

17:42.809 --> 17:44.046
What's this?

17:44.114 --> 17:45.786
This is the bathroom
at my work.

17:45.854 --> 17:46.857
That's right.

17:46.925 --> 17:48.463
And there you are
in the stall

17:48.531 --> 17:49.869
with your boss, Angela.
What?!

17:49.938 --> 17:51.944
Oh, my God, Angela.

17:52.011 --> 17:54.521
That was... that was...
that felt so good.

17:54.589 --> 17:57.097
All I want to do is
please you, Griffin.

17:57.165 --> 17:59.273
Well that... that was
a good idea you had

17:59.341 --> 18:01.448
dunking your hand
in the toilet.

18:01.515 --> 18:03.356
Oh, my God! I wouldn't
have sex with Angela!

18:03.423 --> 18:04.661
She's disgusting!

18:04.728 --> 18:06.200
Not when you're drunk,
she's not.

18:06.268 --> 18:07.472
All right, Death,
I get it.

18:07.539 --> 18:08.911
I wish I'd never
touched a drop

18:08.979 --> 18:10.181
of alcohol in my life.

18:10.250 --> 18:11.554
Never touched
a drop, huh?

18:11.622 --> 18:12.826
Well, guess what.

18:12.894 --> 18:14.366
I'm going to show you
that, too.

18:14.433 --> 18:16.340
(whooshing)

18:18.014 --> 18:19.585
Okay, get ready for this.

18:19.653 --> 18:21.828
Hey, hey, hey, gang!

18:21.896 --> 18:23.669
Everybody line up
for a triple "H":

18:23.737 --> 18:27.952
a hug, a handshake
or a high five. Your call.

18:28.021 --> 18:30.931
Lois, hug--
you got it.

18:30.999 --> 18:33.207
Stewie, hug--
two in a row.

18:33.274 --> 18:34.946
Try for three, Chris?

18:35.015 --> 18:36.687
Oh, no, high five.

18:36.755 --> 18:39.464
Well, that's okay.
High five's great, too.

18:39.532 --> 18:41.472
Meg, back to the hug.
All right.

18:41.540 --> 18:43.079
Hugs may win it today.

18:43.147 --> 18:45.053
And we close
with a handshake.

18:45.120 --> 18:48.367
And all in time for my big
bike ride announcement.

18:48.435 --> 18:50.340
Who the (bleep)
is this jerk?

18:50.408 --> 18:53.085
That's you, Peter,
alcohol-free.

18:53.153 --> 18:54.925
(whooshing)

18:57.536 --> 18:58.506
(both laughing)

18:58.574 --> 19:00.078
Ooh.

19:00.147 --> 19:01.317
Hey, look, there's
Joe and Quagmire.

19:01.385 --> 19:02.690
Hey, let's have a
drink with them.

19:02.757 --> 19:04.161
You've never touched
a drop, Peter.

19:04.230 --> 19:05.902
You don't even know
those guys.

19:05.970 --> 19:08.210
<i>Those are your
friends over there.</i>

19:08.278 --> 19:10.118
Hey, do you guys mind
keeping it down?

19:10.186 --> 19:12.227
We're trying to have
a conversation here.

19:12.295 --> 19:15.005
Some people. Gee whiz.

19:15.072 --> 19:17.714
Those are your friends,
Phillip, Ernest and Jonathan.

19:17.782 --> 19:19.924
Do I at least
call him Jon?

19:19.991 --> 19:21.530
No, he prefers
Jonathan.

19:21.598 --> 19:23.738
Aw, one of those guys?

19:23.806 --> 19:25.412
You know, I have started taking

19:25.480 --> 19:27.253
a Bufferin baby aspirin
every day.

19:27.321 --> 19:29.662
It's improved my heart
one heck of a heap,

19:29.730 --> 19:31.336
I'll tell you that,
pardon my French.

19:31.403 --> 19:33.176
This is even worse
than the other one.

19:33.244 --> 19:34.749
I mean, it's cool
I know French,

19:34.817 --> 19:35.853
but, Death,
this ain't me.

19:35.921 --> 19:37.157
What am I
supposed to do?

19:37.225 --> 19:38.932
If I'm a drunk,
I'm a jerk,

19:39.000 --> 19:40.438
and if I'm sober,
I'm a douche.

19:40.506 --> 19:41.542
Exactly, Peter.

19:41.610 --> 19:42.880
It's called moderation.

19:42.949 --> 19:45.792
You don't have to give up
the booze cold turkey.

19:45.861 --> 19:47.632
You just have to be
responsible with it.

19:47.700 --> 19:49.407
You members of the human race

19:49.474 --> 19:51.683
have the ability
to send a man to the moon

19:51.749 --> 19:54.159
and make Justin Long
a movie star.

19:54.226 --> 19:56.702
With that kind of willpower,
don't you think you can learn

19:56.769 --> 19:59.279
to put the bottle down
just sometimes?

19:59.347 --> 20:01.722
We did it with Justin Long,
didn't we?

20:01.789 --> 20:03.763
America said no,
but we kept at it.

20:03.831 --> 20:05.203
All right, Death.

20:05.270 --> 20:06.406
I'll try.

20:19.493 --> 20:20.831
Well, we're home.

20:20.899 --> 20:23.875
30 days of sobriety,
and we can finally drink again.

20:23.944 --> 20:25.315
Oh, for God's sake, Peter,

20:25.383 --> 20:27.122
didn't you learn
anything from this?

20:27.190 --> 20:29.063
Yes, I did, Lois.

20:29.131 --> 20:31.070
These are going
in the garbage.

20:31.138 --> 20:33.481
But these...
I'm keeping for myself.

20:33.548 --> 20:35.154
Moderation, Lois.

20:35.222 --> 20:36.425
Wow, Peter.

20:36.493 --> 20:38.098
I never thought
I'd see the day.

20:38.166 --> 20:39.738
Good for you.

20:39.807 --> 20:41.578
From now on, half
of every six-pack I buy

20:41.646 --> 20:43.520
is going in the trash.

20:48.507 --> 20:50.513
Hey, how... how come
we're the only animals

20:50.582 --> 20:52.589
with poo that's white?

20:52.657 --> 20:54.430
I know.
What the hell?

20:54.498 --> 20:56.872
Right? We're not... we're
not eating white stuff.

20:56.941 --> 20:58.546
Hey, you want
something good?

20:58.614 --> 21:01.624
Just look for the containers
that say "KFC" on them.

21:01.693 --> 21:03.565
There's always
something good in there.

21:03.634 --> 21:05.104
Dude, that's
birds in there.

21:05.172 --> 21:07.213
You're eat... you're
eating another bird.

21:07.281 --> 21:09.154
What?
That's bird meat, dude.

21:09.222 --> 21:10.793
Wh-what? No.

21:10.861 --> 21:11.932
You're eating a bird.

21:12.000 --> 21:14.208
Oh, my God. Oh, my God!
(squawks)

21:14.209 --> 22:15.209
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru